# Review routing. CODEOWNERS makes the review rules in CONTRIBUTING.md
# platform-visible: GitHub auto-requests these reviewers on any PR touching
# the matched paths, and branch protection (when enabled with "require review
# from Code Owners") makes the request blocking rather than advisory.
#
# An unknown username here fails SILENTLY — GitHub skips it without warning —
# so every entry below is a verified account, and adding a maintainer means
# verifying the handle before committing it.
#
# Later rules override earlier ones; the last match wins.

# Default: everything routes to the maintainer.
* @scott-wyatt

# THE NORMATIVE SURFACE — the paths where a change can alter what conformance
# means. CONTRIBUTING.md requires two maintainer approvals and a version bump
# here (pre-production exception: the bump may be skipped, the approvals may
# not). Listed separately so that when a second maintainer exists, adding
# them to THESE lines is the one-line change that makes the two-approval rule
# enforceable, and so a reviewer can see at a glance that a PR has crossed
# from editorial into normative territory.
/spec/aph-0.1.md @scott-wyatt
/spec/a2a-extension.md @scott-wyatt
/spec/schemas/ @scott-wyatt
/examples/ @scott-wyatt

